data srv1_floor_memory_budget_live_note: String = "Floor width sizing reads the LIVE slot cap (gunbc_ci_runner_slot_memory_max_live, converge receipt 2026-07-05: 24GiB hand-set on the hosts), not the declared 8GiB gunbc_runner_slot_desired row - per the live row's own consumer guidance ('consumers sizing within-run compile parallelism read ..._live until the converge dissolve closes'). Forced by the 2026-07-09 discovery flip: the corpus batch's measured executor base overhead (~8.3GiB, gunbc_ci_floor_executor_base_overhead) structurally cannot fit the declared 8GiB slot at any width, so sizing against the declared row would floor the width fold at its saturation arm; the executor's runtime cgroup read (the actual OOM authority) is the live value anyway. Dissolve-on: same trigger as the live row - converge proves live == declared, collapse to the gunbc.runner_slot_allocation single authority."
