data srv1_floor_memory_budget_live_note: String = "Floor width sizing reads the LIVE slot cap (gunbc_ci_runner_slot_memory_max_live, converge receipt 2026-07-05: 24GiB hand-set on the hosts), not the declared gunbc_runner_slot_desired row (16GiB per the 2026-07-10 operator ruling; 8GiB when this note was authored) - per the live row's own consumer guidance ('consumers sizing within-run compile parallelism read ..._live until the converge dissolve closes'). Originally forced by the 2026-07-09 discovery flip: the corpus batch's measured executor base overhead (~8.3GiB, gunbc_ci_floor_executor_base_overhead) structurally could not fit the then-declared 8GiB slot at any width; at the 16GiB declaration width-1 fits (~14.7GiB = base + one shard), but the executor's runtime cgroup read (the actual OOM authority) remains the live value until converge applies the ruling. Dissolve-on: same trigger as the live row - converge proves live == declared, collapse to the gunbc.runner_slot_allocation single authority."
